target: internal/record/record.go
verify: go test ./internal/record/ -count=1 -run 'TestDroppedGatesCollapsesTheFalsyStatusesAStringCanHold'
expect: gate g_empty reported
why:    RESTORED, narrowed. This entry was retired as "now unreachable", which was wrong: typing turned `false`/`0`/`null` into decode errors, but the EMPTY STRING is still a status a string can hold, the collapse that handles it is still live code (`res.Status != nil && *res.Status != ""`), and after the retirement no catalog entry mutated that collapse at all. Defaulting only on ABSENCE reports "" as the gate's status, and an empty status names nothing about the gate — the status is the whole content of the alarm line. The Python's `st or "unreported"` collapses all of them.
